				<wikidot:authorName>Taffeta</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2221240</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;I&nbsp;dunno.</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Spoilers.</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>The main character is assigned to <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/crossoverprojectindex">Crossover</a> between <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/canon-hub">Alternate</a> <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AlternateUniverse">Universes</a>, uncovers the murder of a woman killed due to an Inconsistent<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-754809-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Headcanon">Head Cannon</a>. Her unwilling Collaborator is a <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CanonWelding">Canon Welder</a><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-754809-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup> who has a copy (an <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Expy">Expy</a>, shall we say) of the dead character in the Alternate Universe where she doesn't die, revealing she's <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OnlyMostlyDead">Only Mostly Dead</a>.</p> </div> </div> </div> <p>What do you think they have to do with one another?</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-754809-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. origins-wise, is it Orthodoxy or Maxwellist?</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-754809-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. among other duties</div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
